Add a cargo-fuzz target `ndjson` (upstream has none)

A lean4export NDJSON stream checked as the arena runs `scripts/arena-run
FILE 4` (susz pack --no-index, then gruszka FILE.susz), on one worker on
the calling thread: packed in memory by susz 0.1.4 (the arena's packer),
loaded, and checked in file order to the first failure, with the
overflow-arena rerun of main.rs. gruszka's lockfile pins susz 0.1.1 for
reading; the fuzz crate reads with the patched 0.1.4 as well (read.rs and
index.rs are identical, canon.rs and format.rs differ in a few lines, and
0.1.1 does not build for wasm32 either). The deliberate "a worker table
is full" panic ends the test case through wasmfuzz's exit_testcase; every
other panic is a finding (main.rs would decline with "internal error").
Upstream: none (no fuzz targets upstream, checked 2026-11-22).

